    {
      "number": 1016,
      "title": "task: recover a stranded Task Session without human intervention",
      "body": "## Usage\n\n```bash\ncargo test -p loopflow child_session\ncargo test -p loopflow ops::task\n```\n\nA Task Session whose durable status still claims a live body — but whose body is gone — used to sit frozen until a human noticed and swept it by hand. Supervision now classifies that strand structurally and redispatches it on its own, bounded to a fixed number of consecutive attempts before it stops and says why.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe existing recovery path only fired on *stalls* — a body that was alive but not progressing. A body that died without recording an outcome left nothing to stall on, so the Session froze at its last generation and no supervision pass would ever touch it again. This adds a second classifier, `plan_stranded_recovery`, for the bodyless case, plus the dispatcher that acts on it.\n\nThe classification is keyed on durable **status** (via `BodyIntent`), never on the `lost` label alone: a Task that completed successfully *also* reaps its body as `lost`, so anything keyed on the tag by itself chases finished work forever. Intent is consulted first and rejects terminal and deliberately-parked work before the outcome tag is read at all. That is also what preserves the open-PR bar without ever consulting the PR phase — delivered work parks at `Waiting`, which is never stranded.\n\nEvery lease state and outcome gets an explicit arm rather than a fall-through, since a missed case silently strands a whole class of body:\n\n- `lost` / a dead body still holding its lease → recoverable, redispatch\n- `superseded` still sitting on the latest generation → an intended recovery that aborted; redispatch\n- `failed` → the body recorded why it stopped; surface that reason instead of blindly re-failing\n- a lease stuck at `revoked` → a reap that never finished; no new generation can ever be reserved, so surface the real cause instead of burning the attempt budget on an impossible CAS\n- `completed` / `interrupted` / legacy stops → leave alone\n\n## Changes\n\n- `plan_stranded_recovery` + `strand_verdict` in `child_session.rs`, with a test per row of the truth table\n- `count_recovery_attempts` bounds retries progress-relatively: lease/status/failure churn is what a recovery itself writes, so only real work resets the budget. A failed launch counts as churn — otherwise an unlaunchable Session would reset its budget on every attempt and retry forever.\n- Attempts are bounded on their own counter rather than the process generation, which also increments on legitimate PR rotation\n- New `BodyRecoveryAttempted` task event, surfaced in chat activity\n- Dispatcher in `ops/task.rs`; skips reservations still inside their startup grace so an in-flight relaunch isn't double-dispatched",
      "files": [],
      "additions": 925,
      "deletions": 27,
      "changed_files": 7
    },
    {
      "number": 1017,
      "title": "trace: make missing capture artifacts explicitly terminal",
      "body": "Adds operator-driven lf runs reconcile tombstones for capture artifacts removed out of band while keeping fresh loss a doctor failure. Trace roots now follow the Home that owns the store, pruned launches remain attributable for accounting, and migration/reconciliation tests preserve every historical row and index.",
      "files": [],
